This Python program calculates the minimum number of substrings that need to be reversed to restore the original string. However, it requires O(n^3) time complexity due to re-computing min(dp[i + j][i + j - (end - j)]) for every start and end, which is too slow for large inputs. A more efficient algorithm based on dynamic programming with memorization or tabulation may be required for larger inputs.

